# Request to inspect and review education records under FERPA

To whom it may concern,

I am a student at {{ institution }}{% if student.programme %}, enrolled in {{ student.programme }}{% endif %}{% if student.student_id %} (student ID {{ student.student_id }}){% endif %}. Under the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act, 20 U.S.C. § 1232g, and 34 CFR § 99.10, I request to inspect and review the education records directly related to me that concern the checking of my work{% if request.submission_title %} "{{ request.submission_title }}"{% endif %}{% if request.course %} for {{ request.course }}{% endif %}{% if submission_date %}, submitted on {{ submission_date }}{% endif %}{% if tools %}, including any checks made with {{ tools | join(", ") }}{% endif %}.

Specifically, I ask to inspect and review:

1. Every similarity report and every AI-writing report generated for this work and maintained by the institution or by a party acting for it, including the matched sources, the matched passages and the settings applied.
2. Any notes, assessments, emails or decisions concerning me that rely on those reports, including any referral to the Dean of Students or a conduct office.
3. Any record showing whether my work was added to a vendor's repository of submitted papers.
{% for item in request.extra_items %}
{{ loop.index + 3 }}. {{ item }}
{% endfor %}

Under 34 CFR § 99.10(c), I also ask for a reasonable explanation and interpretation of these records, including what the reported scores mean and how they were used.

Please let me know when and where I can inspect the records, or send copies electronically. FERPA requires access within a reasonable time and no later than {{ duration(deadline) }} after receipt of this request, and no fee may be charged to search for or retrieve the records (34 CFR § 99.11).

Sincerely,

{{ student.name }}
